{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"1. **Frame pacing / jank**\n- Run in profile mode: `flutter run --profile --trace-skia`\n- Capture frame stats during a 60s avatar interaction:  \n  `adb shell dumpsys gfxinfo <package> framestats > framestats.txt`\n- Check jank ratio and slow frames (`>16ms`, `>33ms`, `>50ms`) from `framestats.txt`; fail if janky frames trend upward between builds or exceed ~5% in steady state.\n- Record a system trace for UI/GPU correlation:  \n  `adb shell perfetto -o /data/misc/perfetto-traces/avatar.pftrace -t 20s sched freq idle gfx view binder_driver hal dalvik`  \n  `adb pull /data/misc/perfetto-traces/avatar.pftrace`\n- In trace, verify no repeating long gaps between `Choreographer` frame deadlines and render completion.\n\n2. **Lifecycle resume rendering reliability**\n- Stress home/resume cycles (20x):  \n  `adb shell input keyevent KEYCODE_HOME`  \n  `adb shell monkey -p <package> -c android.intent.category.LAUNCHER 1`\n- Stress pause/resume via screen off/on (20x):  \n  `adb shell input keyevent KEYCODE_POWER` (off)  \n  `adb shell input keyevent KEYCODE_POWER` (on)  \n  `adb shell input swipe 300 1000 300 300` (unlock gesture if needed)\n- During loop, stream lifecycle + GL logs:  \n  `adb logcat | findstr /i \"ActivityTaskManager Flutter GLSurfaceView onPause onResume Surface\"`\n- After each resume, re-check frame production:  \n  `adb shell dumpsys gfxinfo <package> framestats`  \n  fail if frame counters stop advancing, black frame persists, or first-frame-after-resume latency regresses build-to-build.\n\n3. **Memory pressure regressions**\n- Baseline + post-15min-run memory snapshots:  \n  `adb shell dumpsys meminfo <package> > mem_before.txt`  \n  `adb shell dumpsys meminfo <package> > mem_after.txt`\n- Track key deltas: `TOTAL PSS`, `Native Heap`, `Graphics`, `EGL mtrack`, `GL mtrack`; fail if monotonic growth does not recover after GC/resume cycles.\n- Force pressure signal and verify survival/recovery:  \n  `adb shell am send-trim-memory <package> RUNNING_CRITICAL`\n- Re-check after trim + resume:  \n  `adb shell dumpsys meminfo <package>`  \n  fail if avatar render fails to recover or native/graphics memory spikes permanently.\n\n4. **CPU/GPU overuse symptoms**\n- Sample process CPU while avatar animates:  \n  `adb shell top -H -p $(adb shell pidof <package>) -d 1`\n- Watch render thread/raster thread for sustained high CPU; fail if sustained near-core saturation in steady scenes.\n- Check device thermal throttling state:  \n  `adb shell dumpsys thermalservice`\n- Correlate with frame drops under load; fail if jank starts only after thermal severity increases.\n- Inspect GPU/graphics pressure signals:  \n  `adb shell dumpsys gfxinfo <package>`  \n  `adb shell dumpsys SurfaceFlinger --latency`\n- Fail criteria: increasing missed deadlines, rising frame latency percentiles, and CPU/GPU load staying high after interaction stops."}}
